<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uthman Dey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1610">1610</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uthman Dey was dey of Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> from 1598 until his death in 1610, when deys chosen from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> corps held real power. He organised the administration and the corsair fleet and welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> refugees expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from 1609, who founded towns and introduced crafts and irrigation methods. He was succeeded by his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-dey">Yusuf Dey</a>.</p></div>
